WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.725
Get this right first, because
every other rule depends on it.

2
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:07.580
A GCC Moderate tenant uses
the worldwide endpoints,

3
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.525
the same as a commercial
tenant: Learn says so plainly.

4
00:00:11.525 --> 00:00:15.008
GCC was built when Microsoft
had one cloud directory,

5
00:00:15.008 --> 00:00:17.937
and it still uses that
commercial directory.

6
00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:22.836
It's GCC High and the Department of
Defense cloud that have their own hosts,

7
00:00:22.836 --> 00:00:25.888
for tokens, for Graph
and for Resource Manager.

8
00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:29.199
And a token from one cloud
simply doesn't work in another.

9
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.114
The slide maps all four clouds,

10
00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:34.780
including the PowerShell
environment names you'll pass.
